# PrintPress GH — Cursor Rules

## Project
Multi-role web app for a Ghana print press company.
React + Vite (JavaScript, not TypeScript), React Router v6, Supabase, Tailwind CSS.

## Stack
- React functional components only, no class components
- React Router v6 for all navigation
- Supabase for auth, database, realtime, and file storage
- Tailwind CSS for all styling — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- Mobile-first responsive design on every component

## File structure
- src/components/ — shared reusable UI
- src/pages/ — one file per lobby (CS, Production, Designer, Accounts, Customer, Admin)
- src/lib/ — supabase.js client and helper functions
- src/layouts/ — wrapper layouts (AuthLayout, DashboardLayout)

## Conventions
- All Supabase calls go in src/lib/, never directly inside components
- Use named exports for components
- Keep each page file focused on one lobby only
- Always handle loading and error states visibly
- Quotes and job data shape comes from PrintQuoteGH.jsx — preserve all field names

## Commands
- npm run dev — dev server at localhost:5173
- npm run build — production build
